1
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:31,000
In him,

2
00:01:31,719 --> 00:01:32,640
I saw that

3
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:36,239
my books truly hold some kind of power.

4
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:39,879
It's my genes,

5
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,079
his mission.

6
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,599
My name is Bie Fan.

7
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:51,519
I'm a fan of Mr. Fang.

8
00:01:51,719 --> 00:01:53,959
His books kept me company growing up.

9
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,760
He's the one who got me through

10
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:57,879
the toughest days of my life.

11
00:01:58,040 --> 00:01:58,959
But...

12
00:02:05,359 --> 00:02:06,359
but...

13
00:02:06,879 --> 00:02:09,439
his depression is completely fake.

14
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:12,840
I just heard him say he's fine.

15
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:15,879
These fans are totally brainless.

16
00:02:15,879 --> 00:02:17,639
Just like that Bie Fan.

17
00:02:17,639 --> 00:02:18,840
They aren't very bright either.

18
00:02:19,159 --> 00:02:20,360
The second he cries,

19
00:02:21,199 --> 00:02:23,560
everyone believes he really has depression.

20
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,520
Then he can sell his books.

21
00:02:45,439 --> 00:02:46,080
Mr. Fang.

22
00:02:46,439 --> 00:02:47,879
I know you must be feeling

23
00:02:47,879 --> 00:02:49,240
very, very upset right now.

24
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,719
You're a man of letters, right?

25
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,080
But they made you take off your pants,

26
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,080
eat sausages,

27
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,639
and shave your beard.

28
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,159
You've been through a lot.

29
00:02:56,639 --> 00:02:57,719
But what I want to say is,

30
00:02:58,360 --> 00:03:00,280
all the crap we take today,

31
00:03:00,439 --> 00:03:01,319
we will one day

32
00:03:01,319 --> 00:03:02,719
make them pay back in spades.

33
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,120
Just like you, since I was a kid,

34
00:03:05,439 --> 00:03:06,719
I've always loved literature.

35
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,479
I know how hard it's been

36
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:09,240
for you to get this far.

37
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:09,800
So...

38
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,599
It's been tough, bro.

39
00:03:14,599 --> 00:03:15,919
Here's the thing, Mr. Fang,

40
00:03:16,479 --> 00:03:17,639
let me show you something else.

41
00:03:18,639 --> 00:03:19,400
This

42
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:21,000
is Bie Fan's previous live stream data.

43
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,759
300,000 concurrent viewers.

44
00:03:22,759 --> 00:03:23,719
Trending at the top!

45
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,960
"Fang Haowen fan saves a life by jumping off a bridge"

46
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,759
That's got tens of millions of views.

47
00:03:27,759 --> 00:03:28,280
Just listen to that.

48
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:29,479
Most importantly, Mr. Fang,

49
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:32,039
your book, What Is Success?

50
00:03:32,039 --> 00:03:33,599
sold over 20,000 copies in just an hour.

51
00:03:33,599 --> 00:03:35,039
How many copies that book sells...

52
00:03:35,039 --> 00:03:36,639
what does it have to do with me?

53
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:40,719
Jin Furong is exploiting me, don't you get it?

54
00:03:41,639 --> 00:03:43,039
I want this book to sell well,

55
00:03:43,039 --> 00:03:44,280
don't you guys get it?

56
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:46,080
I get it, we all get it. So,

57
00:03:46,319 --> 00:03:48,960
isn't this grand live stream event

58
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:51,240
called Farewell Rehearsal: Upgraded Edition?

59
00:03:51,719 --> 00:03:53,360
We're going to use this live stream

60
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:54,759
to promote your new book,

61
00:03:54,759 --> 00:03:57,039
and slap them in the face with it!

62
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,240
Tell me, tell me.

63
00:03:59,240 --> 00:03:59,960
With this level of hype,

64
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:00,879
what's the minimum we could sell?

65
00:04:00,879 --> 00:04:02,240
Tell me! Give it to me!

66
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,120
300,000.

67
00:04:04,319 --> 00:04:06,800
Mr. Fang, are you happy with this number?

68
00:04:09,439 --> 00:04:10,120
Come on, give us a smile.

69
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:12,319
Smile.

70
00:04:14,319 --> 00:04:15,879
I... I thought it was just...

71
00:04:16,079 --> 00:04:17,319
I just wanted to be a little dramatic.

72
00:04:20,439 --> 00:04:22,040
Who... who smashed this computer?

73
00:04:22,959 --> 00:04:24,319
300,000! 300,000!

74
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:25,600
How many copies your book sells...

75
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,920
what does that have to do with me?

76
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:28,560
Next time you show someone data,

77
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:29,839
could you use your own computer?

78
00:04:31,199 --> 00:04:31,959
Psycho.

79
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:53,759
Ms. He,

80
00:04:54,399 --> 00:04:56,519
why did Mr. Fang commit suicide?

81
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,120
To tell you the truth,

82
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:05,360
Mr. Fang has a very serious illness

83
00:05:06,399 --> 00:05:07,680
called depression.

84
00:05:09,319 --> 00:05:10,680
So you have to...

85
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:12,879
You have to help him more.

86
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:14,240
If you encourage him more,

87
00:05:14,519 --> 00:05:16,480
it'll ease his pain a bit.

88
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,600
Depression?

89
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:20,879
He's totally doomed then.

90
00:05:20,879 --> 00:05:21,879
That's hard to cure.

91
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,000
Remember back in our village,

92
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,839
there was a cow named Fangfang?

93
00:05:24,839 --> 00:05:26,000
Didn't she die of an illness?

94
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:27,680
Her calf got depressed.

95
00:05:27,839 --> 00:05:29,120
The meat was super tough.

96
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,399
Didn't you eat some too?

97
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,680
What's up? Whose cow is depressed?

98
00:05:34,439 --> 00:05:36,399
What are the symptoms of depression?

99
00:05:36,839 --> 00:05:37,680
Symptoms?

100
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,680
Crying. Crying over nothing.

101
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,480
Their mood is just terrible.

102
00:05:44,079 --> 00:05:44,959
Let me tell you,

103
00:05:44,959 --> 00:05:46,879
being short-tempered is an illness too.

104
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:51,480
The worst is when they're always smiling.

105
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:53,240
It's called smiling depression.

106
00:05:53,759 --> 00:05:54,439
Hard to cure.

107
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,600
You have no idea when he's actually happy

108
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,519
or when he's not.

109
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:59,240
What's up? Whose cow...

110
00:06:03,519 --> 00:06:06,399
Then what can I do for Mr. Fang?

111
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:08,959
Nail this live stream.

112
00:06:09,879 --> 00:06:11,839
Memorize the lines I gave you.

113
00:06:12,199 --> 00:06:13,759
As long as you don't drop the ball on stream,

114
00:06:14,199 --> 00:06:15,759
Mr. Fang will get better.

115
00:06:17,879 --> 00:06:18,720
Memorize them well.

116
00:06:19,199 --> 00:06:20,480
I definitely will.

117
00:06:20,839 --> 00:06:22,199
Mr. Bie Fan, Mr. Fang.

118
00:06:22,199 --> 00:06:23,600
We can head to the rehearsal now.

119
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:25,040
Let's go.

120
00:06:25,879 --> 00:06:26,560
This way, please.

121
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:27,240
Let's go. Let's go.

122
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:30,600
Mr. Fang...

123
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:33,000
I know you're happy,

124
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:35,319
but stop grinning all the time.

125
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:36,759
What do you mean?

126
00:06:37,759 --> 00:06:40,120
I read your second book.

127
00:06:41,319 --> 00:06:43,279
Well, that makes me pretty happy. Was it good?

128
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:45,480
Well...

129
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:49,000
it didn't seem as good as the first one.

130
00:06:50,639 --> 00:06:51,759
Now I'm upset.

131
00:06:53,839 --> 00:06:55,040
No, please don't be.

132
00:06:55,279 --> 00:06:56,519
I'll keep reading.

133
00:06:56,519 --> 00:06:58,600
It might get better later.

134
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:02,240
I guess so.

135
00:07:02,959 --> 00:07:04,360
To you, this second book

136
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:06,639
is indeed hard to grasp.

137
00:07:08,319 --> 00:07:09,639
These little poems are mostly

138
00:07:09,879 --> 00:07:12,040
my reflections on life.

139
00:07:13,399 --> 00:07:16,079
Is that why you got sick?

140
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,040
You... you...

141
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:21,959
You'll understand if you read slowly.

142
00:07:21,959 --> 00:07:25,360
My mom says, "Cure it if you're sick.

143
00:07:25,639 --> 00:07:26,839
Prevent it if you're healthy."

144
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:28,879
Your mom is right.

145
00:07:29,959 --> 00:07:30,639
Isn't this great?

146
00:07:30,639 --> 00:07:31,360
Pretty healthy, right?

147
00:07:33,279 --> 00:07:34,480
Thanks for trusting me.

148
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:35,920
And coming to the live stream with me.

149
00:07:36,519 --> 00:07:37,920
After my second book is published,

150
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:39,160
I'll give you a copy.

151
00:07:39,639 --> 00:07:40,920
And write you a nice dedication.

152
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:45,279
I'll treasure the book you sign for me.

153
00:07:45,639 --> 00:07:47,839
I'll place it right next to my mom's ashes.

154
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:50,759
Mr. Bie Fan.

155
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,639
Mr. Bie Fan.

156
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:55,360
Can we go over the script now?

157
00:07:57,639 --> 00:08:00,079
Y-You don't need to call me Mr.

158
00:08:00,319 --> 00:08:02,240
They all call me Master Bie.

159
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:06,160
Okay, Mr. Master Bie.

160
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,240
Can we head over there now

161
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:09,079
to go over the script?

162
00:08:10,759 --> 00:08:11,000
Sure.

163
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,199
We should go over the script. Let's go.

164
00:08:12,199 --> 00:08:13,560
Going over the script is fine.

165
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,480
This way, this way. Don't be nervous.

166
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,480
We do need to go over the script.

167
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:19,120
Mr. Fang!

168
00:08:19,279 --> 00:08:21,360
Over here, here, here!

169
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:25,879
Let me walk you through the rundown first.

170
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:28,839
When the live stream kicks off,

171
00:08:28,959 --> 00:08:30,560
the first thing they'll see

172
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:32,440
are four beautiful dancers.

173
00:08:32,639 --> 00:08:36,200
They will represent The Four Arts,

174
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:38,279
which symbolize Mr. Fang's talent,

175
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:40,519
all-encompassing!

176
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:45,120
My brain

177
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:47,919
isn't working well.

178
00:08:48,679 --> 00:08:51,080
Mr. Master Bie, come hit your mark.

179
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,559
This balcony up here

180
00:08:54,559 --> 00:08:56,519
was custom-built just for you.

181
00:08:56,519 --> 00:08:58,840
A 1:1 replica of your home!

182
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,679
To correct your slip

183
00:09:01,559 --> 00:09:04,200
and fall from that day!

184
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,960
You'll descend like the God of Literature

185
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,519
slowly from above.

186
00:09:09,639 --> 00:09:11,279
Don't worry, the wire is very safe.

187
00:09:11,279 --> 00:09:11,960
Haowen.

188
00:09:12,399 --> 00:09:13,320
What do you think?

189
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,840
How's the set design?

190
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,679
Wasn't much, just a few hundred thousand.

191
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:19,480
Any other questions? Just ask!

192
00:09:19,759 --> 00:09:20,840
Everything else is fine.

193
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,639
Right, um, earlier,

194
00:09:22,639 --> 00:09:23,639
you mentioned that...

195
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,799
that thing holding me up, the wi-something?

196
00:09:26,279 --> 00:09:27,000
The wire. The wire.

197
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,200
Is the wire safe?

198
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,440
Are you kidding? Our boss's team

199
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,080
was brought in from Hollywood.

200
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:35,039
Over there, it's US dollars every day.

201
00:09:35,679 --> 00:09:36,600
You earn it, but don't dare spend it.

202
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:37,480
It's pretty boring.

203
00:09:38,679 --> 00:09:39,600
What I mean is,

204
00:09:40,799 --> 00:09:42,320
are we sure this re-wi is safe?

205
00:09:42,879 --> 00:09:43,360
Of course!

206
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:44,919
If something happened, how could we keep working?

207
00:09:46,679 --> 00:09:47,159
Unhook him.

208
00:09:47,279 --> 00:09:48,480
If it's really safe,

209
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,600
do you think later on,

210
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:52,279
you could pull me up a bit higher?

211
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,159
Like, the higher the better.

212
00:09:53,159 --> 00:09:55,279
The higher you pull me, the more dangerous it looks.

213
00:09:55,559 --> 00:09:56,720
And the more dangerous it looks,

214
00:09:57,159 --> 00:09:58,279
the more the audience might pity me.

215
00:09:58,279 --> 00:09:59,360
The more they pity me,

216
00:09:59,519 --> 00:10:00,799
the stronger their desire to buy the book!

217
00:10:01,159 --> 00:10:02,360
Do you know what I mean?

218
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:04,720
You're planning to sell it as your posthumous work, huh?

219
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:06,279
Let me tell you,

220
00:10:06,679 --> 00:10:08,159
back when we were in Hollywood,

221
00:10:08,159 --> 00:10:10,159
for Jet Li and Jackie Chan,

222
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:12,159
we were the ones who decided how high to pull them.

223
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:13,600
Safety first.

224
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,600
It's not a joke.

225
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,039
You think we just pull you as high as you want?

226
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:17,919
Okay, okay, okay.

227
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:22,399
Pangpang, Pangpang, Pangpang.

228
00:10:22,399 --> 00:10:23,279
Hello, Pangpang.

229
00:10:23,279 --> 00:10:24,480
Do we have any drinks here?

230
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:25,600
For our brothers from Yawei.

231
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:26,279
Hand some out.

232
00:10:26,279 --> 00:10:27,600
Okay, I'll pass them out in a bit.

233
00:10:27,799 --> 00:10:28,360
Alright.

234
00:10:28,559 --> 00:10:29,279
Thanks a lot.

235
00:10:29,279 --> 00:10:29,799
No problem.

236
00:10:29,799 --> 00:10:31,159
We're setting this spot right here.

237
00:10:31,159 --> 00:10:31,919
It's not moving.

238
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:32,919
Nobody touch it.

239
00:10:33,919 --> 00:10:36,279
Mr. Fang, I wouldn't tell anyone else this.

240
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,279
You can show off these chicken feet,

241
00:10:39,279 --> 00:10:40,679
but whatever you do, don't eat them.

242
00:10:40,919 --> 00:10:42,840
They were prepped for the bridge jump.

243
00:10:43,279 --> 00:10:44,919
We don't have a fridge. They've gone bad.

244
00:10:44,919 --> 00:10:46,039
Okay, okay. Thanks, bro.

245
00:10:46,039 --> 00:10:46,720
Thanks, thanks.

246
00:10:47,279 --> 00:10:49,159
No worries, we're all family here.

247
00:10:49,159 --> 00:10:49,919
A Zu.

248
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:52,120
Boss Lei's relative.

249
00:10:53,919 --> 00:10:55,039
Let me know if you need anything.

250
00:10:55,039 --> 00:10:55,720
Will do, will do.

251
00:11:01,919 --> 00:11:02,879
Where's the producer?

252
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:03,879
What's up?

253
00:11:04,039 --> 00:11:05,279
I said, where are the box lunches?

254
00:11:05,279 --> 00:11:07,279
We have no energy to dance without food.

255
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:09,600
Big brother, you gotta stand up for us.

256
00:11:09,799 --> 00:11:11,000
We're starving!

257
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:13,559
Wait, how could there not be any?

258
00:11:13,559 --> 00:11:15,080
I remember I didn't just get you box lunches.

259
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:16,960
I even added a big chicken leg for each of you.

260
00:11:19,919 --> 00:11:21,879
Wait, who is it?

261
00:11:23,399 --> 00:11:24,759
So greedy.

262
00:11:25,679 --> 00:11:26,600
Such a glutton.

263
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,559
Don't you know it's one box lunch per person?

264
00:11:28,559 --> 00:11:29,720
So greedy.

265
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:30,799
Who are you talking about?

266
00:11:32,559 --> 00:11:34,120
What the hell are you yelling about?

267
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,080
What about it?

268
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,639
What do you even do here?

269
00:11:37,039 --> 00:11:38,440
What's wrong with me eating?

270
00:11:38,639 --> 00:11:40,000
Eating is fine,

271
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:43,720
but you can't eat four big box lunches!

272
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:46,279
I'm a martial artist.

273
00:11:46,639 --> 00:11:48,039
Nothing wrong with me eating more, right?

274
00:11:48,039 --> 00:11:49,639
I'm Bro Fangtan. You don't know me?

275
00:11:49,639 --> 00:11:51,519
What's so special about Bro Fangtan?

276
00:11:51,519 --> 00:11:52,159
Bro Fangtan or not,

277
00:11:52,159 --> 00:11:53,919
you still can't just eat other people's

278
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:55,120
four big box lunches!

279
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:58,000
What crew preps exact portions with zero extras?

280
00:11:58,039 --> 00:11:59,440
Have you ever even worked on a set?

281
00:11:59,679 --> 00:12:01,279
You're as fat as a pillar.

282
00:12:01,279 --> 00:12:02,639
Go away! Stay back.

283
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:05,320
Producer! Producer!

284
00:12:05,399 --> 00:12:06,320
I am the producer!

285
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:09,879
Alice!

286
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:11,000
Coming, coming.

287
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,039
What's up, bro?

288
00:12:13,159 --> 00:12:14,120
Is this your guy?

289
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:15,840
A Zu, come here.

290
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:16,320
Yeah.

291
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,000
